dual-buffer, flex layers and auto zones for the llama.cpp pin (b12177)

--dual-buffer / LLAMA_ARG_DUAL_BUFFER (and --dual-buffer-pattern, --dual-buffer-limit):
repacked CPU weights are also kept in the host buffer (original format), with an automatic
RAM guard (cgroup aware, placement based estimate).
--flex-layers N / LLAMA_ARG_FLEX_LAYERS: the first N GPU layers can move between GPU and CPU
at runtime (zone 2: repacked copy + host copy; debug trigger: LLAMA_FLEX_TEST).
--auto-zones / LLAMA_ARG_AUTO_ZONES (and --zones-ctx-init / LLAMA_ARG_ZONES_CTX_INIT):
three-zone placement from two --fit runs (dense and MoE), a KV cache that grows with the use
(growable VMM buffers on CUDA/HIP, copy fallback elsewhere; LLAMA_KV_NO_VMM=1 turns VMM off),
and flex layers that go off when the KV needs device memory and come back when it shrinks.
The KV that grows is the cache itself, the non-SWA part of an iswa cache or the attention part of
a hybrid memory (SWA K/V and recurrent state keep their size); with no dynamic KV the flex layers
go off for the full K/V. --zones-margin-mmproj / LLAMA_ARG_ZONES_MARGIN_MMPROJ: the projector part
of the fit target, not kept free again by the zones.
The KV shrinks only as far as flex layers that are off can come back (LLAMA_ZONES_SHRINK=0: never;
LLAMA_ZONES_SHRINK_IDLE=<s>: only after that long without a batch); the experts of a whole flex
layer go off first and come back last; the device compute buffer is booked in the budget.
VMM layout: one address range per device, a section per K/V, fixed size chunks (chosen at load from the granularity, the alignment and the measured driver booking unit; GGML_CUDA_VMM_CHUNK_KIB), shrunk in place (on HIP every chunk has its own address reservation, so the VRAM comes back; runtime memcpy/memset split per reservation),
after mapping a KFD barrier on HIP (GGML_CUDA_VMM_SYNC; a failed barrier falls back to a copy), then synchronous
zeroing; growth steps of one chunk per section; llama_memory_reserve grows the KV for a whole prompt in one step (called by llama-server). GGML_CUDA_VMM_DEBUG=1 logs every reservation, mapping,
access setting, zeroing, growth and release.
Ported from csaki89/llama.cpp (dual-buffer branch, 67df96219, based on e14a77971 = b12140-23)
to the b12177 pin (14 commits later; none of them touches the patched files except common/arg.cpp,
which applies without conflict). The diff is the source diff unchanged. Must be applied after 001
(it touches src/llama-model-loader.cpp as well).

multimodel (csaki89/llama.cpp multimodel 8c1fd95ac): Vulkan chunked growable KV buffers (ordinary device buffers of whole K/V rows; the shaders that read or write the K/V have KV_CHUNKED builds that reach the chunks by their buffer device addresses through a chunk table; chunk from the device: granularity, 2 MiB alignment, measured booking and release units, allocation limit), low-latency split boundaries (one submission and one spinning wait per boundary), ggml_backend_dev_memory_measured / _internal_memory / _host_memory / _async_readback (zones booking, RAM guards, scheduler readback), copy fallback without the whole-KV peak, GGML_SCHED_TIMING, --no-zones-flex, --park / POST /park, /unpark, /park/drop.

